# Subtest: guide: server-needing decorations remain separate
not ok 18 - guide: server-needing decorations remain separate
  ---
  duration_ms: 1.670042
  type: 'test'
  location: '/home/ccheever/sb4-intent/lane-qs/snapback4/packages/snapback4/test/one-shot-review.test.mjs:115:1'
  failureType: 'testCodeFailure'
  error: |-
    The input did not match the regular expression /Keep server-needing decorations separate/. Input:
    
    '# Client: answers stay on screen\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Submit at custody.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```tsx\n' +
      'import { useState } from "react";\n' +
      'import { useMutation, useQuery } from "snapback4/react";\n' +
      'import { existence, isReady } from "snapback4/contract";\n' +
      'import { api } from "../snapback/generated/api";\n' +
      'export function Composer({ conversationId }: { conversationId: string }) {\n' +
      '  const [draft, setDraft] = useState("");\n' +
      '  const send = useMutation(api.send);\n' +
      '  const member = useQuery(api.myMembership, { conversationId });\n' +
      '  const blocked = existence(member) === "denied" || (existence(member) === "absent" && isReady(member) && member.fresh && !member.revalidating);\n' +
      '  const [submitted, setSubmitted] = useState("");\n' +
      '  async function submit() {\n' +
      '    if (blocked) return;\n' +
      '    const text = draft; setSubmitted(text); setDraft("");\n' +
      '    const write = await send.run({ conversationId, body: text }, { waitSeconds: 0 });\n' +
      '    if (write.state === "failed") setDraft(current => current || text);\n' +
      '  }\n' +
      '  return <><input value={draft} onChange={e => setDraft(e.target.value)} />\n' +
      '    <button disabled={send.inFlight || blocked} onClick={() => void submit()}>Send</button>\n' +
      '    {send.last?.state === "failed" && submitted && <p role="alert">Not sent: {submitted} <button onClick={() => setDraft(current => current ? current + " " + submitted : submitted)}>Edit</button> <button onClick={() => setSubmitted("")}>Dismiss</button></p>}</>;\n' +
      '}\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      "Membership with no horizon, synced in the conversation's own group with the messages' audience, proves `present`/`absent` after acquisition unless a pending prediction blocks absence. `loading` means acquisition or later withdrawal. Never add `with own keys` to admin-written memberships.\n" +
      'Queueing needs no membership answer: only `denied`, or fresh, non-revalidating `absent`, disables Send. Stale offline absence still queues; the server authorizes or refuses at sync. `loading`/`partial` never disable.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '`waitSeconds: 0` returns at custody; `inFlight` covers the call, not settlement. After session readiness, acquisition never gates admission. Identity I/O gets 15 seconds excluding prior admissions; `usePendingWrites()` says “not yet admitted”. Reload loses this call. Identification resumes admission in order; `E_ADMISSION_STORE`/`E_ADMISSION_TIMEOUT` permit retry after repair without remounting.\n' +
      'Clear on submit; restore refused text only into an empty draft, otherwise offer Edit/Dismiss. Show “Sending…” on predicted rows (`pending: true`).\n' +
      'Save `{ id: mintId(), args }` in account/backend-scoped storage before `run(args, { id, waitSeconds: 0 })`. `usePendingWrite` shows “Saving…” during submission, “Checking…” while `restoring`; afterward, undefined means unknown. Never automatically resend. Keep saved text; Dismiss only after lookup settles. New attempts get new ids; replay confirms execution without historical results. Web/Expo starters include this journal.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Honest read boundaries\n' +
      '\n' +
      '`query(op, args)` waits for publishable device/server data and app authority: ready or denied, never loading. Retired/expired answers reread: four rounds, 30 seconds including queues/authority (while runnable); exhaustion refuses retryable `E_QUERY_RETRY`. Admitted writes precede ready data. `online only` waits online; offline: permitted device data or immediate `E_OFFLINE`. Closed/signed-out/replaced/restored stores retain their refusals. Ready may be partial/stale; `existence(await query(...))` excludes loading.\n' +
      'Use `existence(read)`; after `isReady(read)`, `read.existence` narrows point data.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '| Meaning | UI decision |\n' +
      '| --- | --- |\n' +
      '| `loading` | No answer yet or withheld: keep composers, headers and routes mounted. |\n' +
      '| `denied` | Refusal: show its message; disable the durable action. |\n' +
      '| `present` | Nonempty top-level value: render it, even with incomplete coverage. |\n' +
      '| `absent` | Proven empty answer: resolve the missing route/row. |\n' +
      '| `partial` | Empty, uncertain answer: show “Partial results”; never infer absence or denial. |\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Only top-level `null`/`[]` is empty; scalars/nested nulls are present. Empty is `absent` only with `complete`, `cut === null`, no `next`, and no admission or intersecting prediction. Unknown prediction footprints block every read; complete local execution narrows dependencies. Precedence: present, absent, partial. `fresh` never demotes; offline `absent` is absence at the acquired watermark. Hidden/missing rows are indistinguishable.\n' +
      'Route on `present`/`absent`, never `loading`/`partial`. Follow `useAuth().state`; reset drafts on account/backend change. Retention grants no authority.\n' +
      'Same-key plain refetch, reconnect, slow reads, transport failure and retry exhaustion retain `revalidating` answers without timeout. Completed replacements recompute existence. Local commits, online receipts, `/changes` and `/sync` bound retention to one non-renewable second; failure/timeout withdraws. Whole server answers can precede sync; older replicas cannot clear pending notifications. `keep: true` adds 30-second subscriber-free linger; `keep: false` withdraws immediately. Keys, deadlines, sign-out, credentials/store/schema resets withdraw; generation changes withdraw before adoption, even without changed tables.\n' +
      'Search with `usePage`: render `page.items`, classify `page.read`; loading items prove nothing. Show “Partial results” for `existence(page.read) === "partial"`; follow `hasMore`/`loadMore`. Unknown unread counts never hide conversations.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Queries in rows\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Wire-equivalent names/arguments share observations per retention policy; object key order is irrelevant. Prefer paging: 1,000 row hooks require 1,000 evaluations per write. Disjoint writes do zero; authorization inputs are dependencies.\n' +
      'At most eight queued observation attempts start per turn, eight remain active; direct queries and timed presence refreshes use separate paths. `keep: false` withdraws before queueing. Queue wait precedes a new episode; retries never renew existing deadlines. Expiry/resets stay immediate. Unrelated writes preserve fallback memory; clock refresh preserves unexpired newer answers.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```tsx\n' +
      'import { useQuery, usePage } from "snapback4/react";\n' +
      'import { api } from "../snapback/generated/api";\n' +
      'function MemberCount({ conversationId }: { conversationId: string }) {\n' +
      '  const members = useQuery(api.members, { conversationId });\n' +
      '  return <span>{"data" in members ? members.data.length : "…"}</span>;\n' +
      '}\n' +
      'function ConversationList() {\n' +
      '  const page = usePage(api.inboxCards, {});\n' +
      '  return <>{page.items.map(row => <span key={row.id}>{row.title} ({row.memberCount})</span>)}\n' +
      '    {page.hasMore && <button onClick={page.loadMore}>More</button>}</>;\n' +
      '}\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Keep decorations separate.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Expo and acquisition\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Every milestone: `npm run export:ios` for Hermes; on a Mac with Xcode, `npm run native:smoke` (about 3 minutes warm). It installs Release and proves local-store acquisition, offline reopen and reconnect. Pending write replay needs an application scenario (`guide witness`).\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Social: `nativeDevice` on native, `webDevice()` on web, online in Expo Go. `guide witness`: native proof; `guide reads`: live timings; `guide sync`: acquisition and offline reopening.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Receipts\n' +
      '\n' +
      '`guide receipts`: schema, mutations, `useReceipts`. SDK owns delivery reporting; the screen owns visible `seen` reporting. Mount above transient rows. “Read” follows foreground newest-message `seen`. Send-time members are recipients; removal claims no reading.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## One-view photos\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Mount **above the list**, keyed by `JSON.stringify([backend, account, messageId, assetId])`. Explicit Open fetches once; recycling/refetch cannot consume or lose the handle. Unmount/account change revokes even late responses. Close on ready `absent`, denied, tombstoned, changed asset or deadline; keep deadlines ticking through loading.\n' +
